    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"### D.3 Interpretation\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **`full_canonical__lgbm`** has the strongest known-domain pooled performance (`pooled_auc \\\\u2248 0.9994`, `fpr \\\\u2248 0.0025`, `ece \\\\u2248 0.0026`). It was, however, trained on a mixed-formula feature set, and its **domain classifier AUC is `1.0`** \\\\u2014 a downstream classifier can perfectly identify which dataset any flow came from. This is a strong indicator of dataset fingerprinting rather than genuine VPN-vs-non-VPN learning.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **`unified_relative_shape_v2__lgbm`** is the recommended runtime candidate. It pays a small offline cost (`test_auc \\\\u2248 0.9826`) but is built on a clean unified feature contract (12 ratio/relative features, identical formulas across ISCX, VNAT, USBVPN, and the live extractor). It has **lower domain fingerprinting** (`domain_auc \\\\u2248 0.959` instead of `1.0`), a **slightly better `lodo_min_auc`** (`\\\\u2248 0.637` vs. `\\\\u2248 0.616` for the legacy baseline), and the **highest `deployment_score`** (`\\\\u2248 0.469`) among all 30 unified candidates.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **`unified_size_shape__lgbm`** is the best low-fingerprint candidate (`domain_auc \\\\u2248 0.948`) but its `lodo_min` (`\\\\u2248 0.562`) is lower than the recommended model.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **`unified_directionless__lgbm`** has the highest pooled AUC among unified candidates (`\\\\u2248 0.996`) but a much lower deployment score, because it scores worse on the transfer / fingerprint axes.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- The unified model is **not production-ready.** Calibration is weak (`ece \\\\u2248 0.30`), FPR at the recommended block threshold is **~7.6%**, and `lodo_min` to ISCX is only **~0.64**. The domain-fingerprinting problem has been **reduced, not solved** \\\\u2014 domain AUC dropped from `1.0` to `\\\\u2248 0.96`, still well above chance.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- The model is suitable for the **simulation firewall** and for thesis claims about methodologically clean evaluation. It must not be used to block real traffic without live-PCAP validation and a recalibration step.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
