    "    \"## H. Remaining limitations\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The recommended model `unified_relative_shape_v2__lgbm` is methodologically clean but **not perfect**.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The thesis must report all of the following honestly:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"1. **Domain fingerprinting is reduced, not eliminated.** Domain classifier AUC dropped from `1.0000` (legacy)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"   to `≈ 0.9591`. A dataset signature is still partially learnable.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"2. **LODO transfer is still weakest on ISCX.** LODO-min ≈ `0.637`. Held-out ISCX flows are the hardest\\n\",\n",
    "    \"   for any model trained on the other two corpora.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"3. **Calibration is mediocre.** Test ECE ≈ `0.299`. Probability values should be interpreted as ranking\\n\",\n",
    "    \"   scores, not as well-calibrated probabilities.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"4. **FPR at the recommended `block` threshold ≈ `0.076`** on the held-out test split. Acceptable for a\\n\",\n",
    "    \"   simulation firewall, not for blocking real users.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"5. **Live PCAP validation:** only the *feature schema* has been confirmed compatible with the live\\n\",\n",
    "    \"   extractor. A full live PCAP evaluation is still required before any production deployment.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"6. **Action mode is `simulation` only.** No packets are blocked.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"7. **USBVPN intake path** uses re-derived features from precomputed statistics (no raw packet arrays\\n\",\n",
    "    \"   available). This is documented in `feature_contract.json`.\\n\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
